        "thinking": "Express is not in node_modules at all, which means the CF package is missing it as a dependency. The server package uses express but the CF package doesn't have it installed. When TypeScript tries to type-check the server route files (which import express), it can't find express types.\n\nBut wait - `hono-adapter.ts` imports from `server/src/http/types.js` which doesn't use express. The difference is that `api.ts` imports from `server/src/routes/companies.js` which imports from `express`. Without express types in node_modules, TypeScript can't type-check those files.\n \nAdding express as a dev dependency to the CF package would solve the type-checking issue, but that feels wrong since we're adding a Node.js dependency to a Workers package. The real issue is that `api.ts` only needs the function signatures from the route factory, not the full Express type system. I should refactor the imports to be more selective about what gets pulled in from the server routes.",
